            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0420" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg348"/>

                <head>No. 180.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Daggett to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 24,
                        1882</date>. (Received October 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that Hon.
                    John Makini Kapena, postmaster-general of the Hawaiian Kingdom, has been
                    appointed envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary to the court of
                    Japan, and will proceed thence at once by way of San Francisco.</p>
                <p>The avowed purpose of his mission is to arrange for bringing Japanese laborers
                    and their families to these islands—a project approved by the sugar planters’
                    union.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROLLIN M. DAGGETT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
